@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+# Sleeper actual-results binding across restoration
+
+Baseline: v1.22.20/build2235,4e63bfbf605c7a1cdd5ce1dc039424e862ab7efd/tree7b2dd610add3a536ba1112f92943ae5ccff5999c.
+
+## Reproduction and narrow cause
+
+Default services.sleeper.load_cache restored week keys and bound native actuals before exposing data. Connected services.league_preparation.restore_cached_runtime restored keys, applied data and published without the binding. Neither publish_cached nor _publish_runtime_context repaired that omission. The correct consumers withheld actuals when the adapter was absent. Using identical compatible retained native rows, the default path supports the source scores while connected restoration reproduces the unavailable-actuals state. The first fixture attempts also exposed ordinary Market asynchronous preparation/isolation assumptions; those original failures are kept separately and the fixture now explicitly completes its normal Market preparation before rendering, without bypassing admission.
+
+This demonstrates a sufficient source-to-screen cause. It does not prove what native rows were in the live Granite cache. Scout's successful build2235 entry and unavailable actuals are supplied observations, not live observations reproduced by this session. A21.00projection is not actual-score parity.
+
+## Shared preparation boundary
+
+services.player_evidence.bind_retained_actuals is used by fresh prepare_player_production, default cache loading and connected cached restoration. It runs before apply_data/publish captures the publication, exactly once per path. It reuses compatible retained preparation, or creates only an empty native-results envelope when preparation is absent/empty and retained matchup evidence exists. It does not read the global analysis store on restoration, acquire sources, calculate fantasy scores, populate a reconstructed fallback or mutate preferences. Foreign league/season/scoring analysis is not relabeled. Existing compatible reference analysis/values and other cached model decisions remain unchanged; cached actual-results disclosures alone are rebound with their existing NOT REVALIDATED qualification for other assessments.
+
+The existing native adapter still resolves explicit player-map/ordered-starter evidence, zero, negatives, conflicts, ownership duplicates, live/completed periods and unknown participation. A missing source generation or known supported-calendar mismatch is now explicitly withheld. Unknown completion can retain explicitly sourced observations as unknown, with no completed windows. Two positive calendar tests previously changed league completion/playoff settings after source preparation; their fixture now republishes identical native rows through the real producer under the declared new calendar. All original assertions remain. Separate mismatched-calendar controls stay negative. Unknown completion remains separately tested without inventing a replacement calendar or final scores.
+
+No new consumer preparation is added. Dossier, Market/API, cached Brain and selected Trade facts read the same admitted envelope and generation. Disclosure reads neither rebind nor fetch. Native clocks are retained; restoration time is not substituted for observation, provider-publication or receipt clocks. A source-generation change without rebinding remains unavailable until an explicit legitimate preparation boundary.
+
+## Numerical and lifecycle acceptance
+
+New rendered-route controls cover the matched paths, missing/empty preparation and pre-adapter atomic caches, foreign scope, calendar/generation mismatch, zero/negative/conflicting scores, missing periods, source clocks, unchanged reference values and cached decisions, binding-before-publication, real canonical context capture, Trade facts, close/reopening, isolated league/scoring contexts and guard-before-binding behavior. Expectations copy retained fixture source scores, not fantasy scoring reconstructed by the implementation.
+
+The optional --native-actuals resource control reuses copies of the sealed prior synthetic source inputs, adding explicitly fictional native matchup rows through the real producer. It does not profile or export a private production payload. Actual2GiB/no-swap/offline controls prove restoration with2,592native observations, including0and-2.125, source-generation agreement, unsafe-pressure deferral before binding, explicit recovery, full FOIS reservation protection, worker exit and scratch cleanup. The original archive remains unchanged and the original build2235 resource case remains required separately. No allowance is reduced.
+
+The2GiB cap,16× restoration allowance, FOIS768MiB and Trade256+128MiB policies, bounded unused-memory recovery, phase ownership, pinned file generation and owned-reader cancellation behavior remain unchanged. Scoring, forward projections, submitted/analytical lineups, exact picks, Neutral/Custom mathematics, saved settings, FOIS provenance and bilateral Trade qualification are untouched.
+
+## Release and live acceptance boundaries
+
+Final-source focused, full local, all ten canonical, all twelve hosted, Product/navigation/security/tooling and constrained resource checks remain mandatory. Original failures, fixture/setup errors and incomplete attempts are separate; deferral never counts as worker completion. Guarded Actions publication must verify exact tree, manifests and immutable attachments before normal deployment.
+
+This session's managed environment has no associated browser-control runtime or Render Shell/SSH execution tool; network policy has no configured VPN/TCP grant. Management reads and public readiness work. The existing external inspection binding401 was not retried because authorization has not demonstrably changed. Main Chat's verified Render-local token200 is supplied evidence, not reproduced here. No credential export, relay or new authentication is introduced.
+
+After deployment, use one existing Render-local preflight, then one normal guarded Granite entry only where fresh evidence permits. Stop on deferral. Compare one supported completed native player-week with the deployed dossier, prepared API/Market and relevant existing fact consumer, pinning league/season/week/scoring/source generation and freshness. The historical26.56Week8capture is only a candidate, not the expected live answer. No forced production sync, Trade search, FOIS rebuild, cache clearing, restart or user-data mutation is authorized for acceptance. Missing live capability must remain HELD rather than be replaced by fixture parity.
+
+## Cancellation validation synchronization
+
+The original full local run recorded a failure in the existing submission-cancellation worker control. Its submission event alone does not establish that the ProcessPool future began executing; canceling a still-queued future may correctly retain the idle pool. The fixture now waits for an explicit marker written by the real spawned worker before canceling. All existing task-drain, worker-exit, scratch-removal and in-flight assertions and time budgets remain. Production FOIS lifecycle code is unchanged. Focused cancellation/timeout controls must pass before the revised source is fully validated. The original run and final traceback remain separate evidence; isolated passes do not erase it.
